<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DEBUG-ONLY overlay of src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml.

  Android resource merging resolves a same-named resource from the variant's own
  build-type source set ahead of src/main, so this file IS the policy for
  `debug` and reaches NO shipping build type (`release`, `storeSafe`, `foss`)
  — testing.md convention 15: the automation surface is compiled out of release
  artifacts. Here the build system's own source-set merge is that boundary
  rather than a release-shrinker fold, which is why the witness is a source-set
  assertion and not an artifact grep:
  tests/e2e-unified/tests/test_android_cleartext_debug_only.py
  derives each shipping type's real directory set from build.gradle.kts, so a
  future srcDir addition that pulled this file into a shipping variant reds
  instead of trusting this comment.

  Why it exists: the e2e harness's default nest mode serves plain
  http://127.0.0.1:[port], and `adb reverse tcp:[p] tcp:[p]` makes that the
  DEVICE's own loopback (tests/e2e-unified/drivers/android.py). Without this, an
  android e2e run cannot complete even its first journey, because every nest
  call dies on the base config's cleartext refusal (testing.md, section
  "Default app and nest mode", Android's run venue, constraint 3).

  127.0.0.1 ONLY. No LAN range, no 10.0.2.2, and base-config is NOT flipped:
  constraint 3 is "production's no-cleartext network policy is never widened",
  and a debug build that trusted a LAN address would put an unauthenticated
  plaintext nest on a network interface, which constraint 2 forbids outright.
  10.0.2.2 (the emulator's alias for its host) is deliberately absent, because
  the reverse tunnel is what carries the device to the nest: the device only
  ever needs its own loopback.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">127.0.0.1</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
